        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Projects/Groups: Big Data, Underworld\n- People: Alan Wilkis, Karl Hyde, Rick Smith\n- Songs/Releases: \"Dangerous\", \"1.0\", \"2.0\", \"Mmm...Skyscraper I Love You\"\n\nFacts:\n- Underworld is a British electronic group formed in 1980 in Cardiff.\n- Underworld is the principal name under which Karl Hyde and Rick Smith have recorded together.\n- \"Mmm...Skyscraper I Love You\" is a 1993 single by Underworld.\n- Big Data is an American electronic music project created by producer Alan Wilkis.\n- \"Dangerous\" is a song by Big Data from the debut EP \"1.0\" released in 2013.\n- \"Dangerous\" is also included on Big Data's debut studio album \"2.0\" released in 2015.",
